Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

## What was implemented:

1. **Fetched Latest Documentation**: Retrieved the most up-to-date Vercel Web Analytics installation instructions from the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart) to ensure compliance with current best practices.

2. **Installed @vercel/analytics Package**: 
   - Added @vercel/analytics@^2.0.1 to the project dependencies
   - Updated package-lock.json with the new package and its dependencies

3. **Configured Analytics Component**:
   - Modified `src/app/layout.tsx` (root layout)
   - Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
   - Placed `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body element, following Next.js App Router best practices

## Files Modified:

- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

## Framework-Specific Implementation:

This project uses **Next.js 16.3.3 with the App Router** architecture. The Analytics component was correctly integrated into the root layout file (`src/app/layout.tsx`) as per the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router projects.

The `<Analytics />` component was placed inside the `<body>` tag, after the `{children}` content, which is the recommended location to track page views and user interactions across all pages of the application.

## Verification Steps Completed:

✅ Build test: Successfully ran `npm run build` - no errors
✅ Linting: Successfully ran `npm run lint` - no errors
✅ Dependencies: Updated lock file properly committed
✅ Code structure: Preserved existing layout structure and styling

## Next Steps for Activation:

To enable Web Analytics on Vercel:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the project's Analytics section in the Vercel dashboard
3. Click the "Enable" button to activate Web Analytics
4. Verify by checking the browser Network tab for requests to the analytics endpoint

## Implementation Notes:

- The Analytics component is framework-aware and will automatically track page views in Next.js
- No additional configuration is required for basic analytics tracking
- The component is lightweight and won't impact page load performance
- Analytics data will be available in the Vercel dashboard once enabled
